the latest CBS News poll finds  Republicans are less likely to wear a  mask in public than Democrats let's take  a look at these numbers they show that  more Republicans 59% described it as a  personal choice while 76% of Democrats  say it is a public health responsibility  our poll also found 62% of Americans  think the u.s. is dealing badly with the  coronavirus and we should note that  nearly all health officials nearly all  health officials recommend wearing a  mask in public it'll keep reports though  on the mixed messages coming from  America's leaders if your local  officials in consultation with the state  are directing you to wear a mask we  encourage everyone to wear a mask  despite vice president pence showing  support for masks on Sunday in an  interview taped Saturday with Face the  Nation he said that he and President  Trump believe is up to local officials  to set the rules we've made it clear  that we want to defer to governor's we  want to defer to local officials the  patchwork of decisions made by state  officials to stretch beyond masks to  testing and reopening and it's leading  to mixed outcomes if I could go back and  redo anything it probably would have  been to slow down the opening of bars we  used science and we wouldn't open any  region unless they hit certain metrics  science shows when people wear masks the  virus doesn't transmit as easily but  across the country there's confusion as  mayor's county leaders and governors all  set different examples in New Jersey  where masks are required in most public  places Democratic governor Phil Murphy  publicly shames constituents on how to  wear one but in Arkansas Republican  governor ASA Hutchinson says a statewide  mandate would be difficult we're not  going to pass a mandate that is  unenforceable from the beginning of the  pandemic mr. Trump has shunned masks but  Democratic presidential candidate Joe  Biden regularly appears in public  wearing a mask he says he'd make it a  national standard one thing we do know  these masks make a gigantic difference  the mixed messages are causing angry  confrontations nationwide like at this  California supermarket on Friday where a  woman refused to wear one saying she had  breathing problems  dr. William Schaffner as a professor of  infectious diseases  this virus knows no political  affiliation it will infect you whether  you're blue red or green vice-president  pence has cancelled campaign appearances  for later this week in Arizona and  Florida but still plans to make official  visits to those states to meet with  their Republican governors the Biden  campaign has no plans to hold  large-scale rallies until they say  public health officials say it's safe to  do so  Anthony ed O'Keefe thank you ad
 

